{
 "_comment": [
  "The GOAL PREDICATE LIBRARY \u2014 task gen's analogue of RoboLab's conditionals.py. DATA, not code:",
  "loaded by agentic_pipeline.load_goal_predicates() and consumed by BOTH task_generator (schema",
  "enum + prompt table + feasibility dispatch) and success.py (which runtime evaluator scores it).",
  "Adding a predicate here makes it selectable by the agent and feasibility-checked \u2014 no code edit.",
  "",
  "TASK GEN CAN PROPOSE EVERY PREDICATE HERE. Scoring is a SEPARATE concern: 'driver' names the",
  "success.py evaluator that measures completion, and is null when no VERIFIED evaluator exists",
  "yet. A null driver does not restrict generation \u2014 the task is ideated normally; its success",
  "simply cannot be scored yet, which success.evaluate() reports explicitly (evaluable=false) and",
  "NEVER papers over by returning a pass.",
  "",
  "The deformable SHAPE evaluators were withdrawn 2026-07-27 after probing each against a",
  "true-success and a true-failure state: every one either false-positived or could never fire.",
  "Common cause: an axis-aligned bounding box cannot express SHAPE or TOPOLOGY. The per-predicate",
  "evidence and the replacement each one needs are in docs/agenticPipeline/success-evaluators.md, deliberately",
  "NOT here, since task gen never needs to read it.",
  "",
  "Fields per predicate:",
  "  params          \u2014 required role names; the agent must supply exactly these (check_static).",
  "  container_param \u2014 which role must be an OPEN-TOP container, or null.",
  "  obj_categories  \u2014 categories the manipulated object may be: THE AFFORDANCE GATE",
  "                    (check_affordance). Gates WHAT the goal may be asked of.",
  "  verb            \u2014 human phrasing, shown to the agent and used in rejection messages.",
  "  attributes      \u2014 RoboLab-style competency tags.",
  "  role_categories \u2014 optional category gate for a non-object role.",
  "  driver          \u2014 success.py evaluator, or null if none is verified yet:",
  "                    open_top_hull | footprint_support | robot_pov_cone  (RoboLab-derived)",
  "                    proximity | separation | robot_reach | height       (generic, verified).",
  "",
  "kind_category maps a catalog entry's 'kind' onto the coarse category obj_categories refers to;",
  "a catalog entry may override it with its own 'category' (a bag is built as cloth physics but",
  "carries category 'bag')."
 ],

